      "edition": "Sunday 1 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad call",
          "heading": "Jake White drafts ex-England international Nathan Hughes into Fiji's Nations squad",
          "body": "Former England international Nathan Hughes returns to the Fiji fold after being drafted into Jake White's 35-man extended squad for the Nations Championship. Hughes, now at Racing 92, last played for England in the 38-38 Six Nations draw with Scotland in 2019. He is one of four uncapped players in the group, alongside Peniami Narisia, Marika Parker and Setareki Bituniyata, all of whom could make their Test debuts this month. Fiji, who beat Japan 34-28 last weekend, begin against France."
        },
