      "edition": "Sunday 1 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad newcomer",
          "heading": "Jamie Benson says Farrell called him into Ireland camp before Ulster move",
          "body": "Jamie Benson, the 24-year-old Ulster back now in Andy Farrell's Nations Championship squad, says Farrell called him into training in July, before he had linked up with the province. \"Obviously, it was a bit of a shock to be called in here before I'd even set foot in Ulster, but it was a great feeling,\" he said. Benson, who came through Richmond and had been in an England A squad, says his Belfast-raised mother was careful not to push him towards Ireland."
        },
