          "kicker": "Australia A tour",
          "heading": "Harry McLaughlin-Phillips scores and creates as Australia A thump USA 52-0",
          "body": "Harry McLaughlin-Phillips, the Bledisloe Cup debutant, scored a try and set up at least three more as Australia A beat the USA Eagles 52-0 in New Jersey, completing a clean sweep of the USA after the opening win in Nashville. McLaughlin-Phillips finished with 17 points, and the forward trio of Nick Frost, Will Harris and Toby Macpherson stole four USA lineouts in the first half. Western Force winger Mac Grealy, whom Les Kiss name-dropped over the weekend, was among several backs with five-pointers."
        },
